{{knowledge_writeback_after_load()}}

## Architecture

```
/resolve (orchestrator - spawns agents only)
│
├─ Phase 0: Worktree Discovery & Pre-flight
├─ Phase 1: Parse issues from TARGET_DIR
<!-- compliance:on -->
├─ Phase 1b: Fetch external threads (evidence policy required)
<!-- compliance:end -->
├─ Phase 2: Global Triage [Triage agent, opus, single agent]
├─ Phase 3: Batch FIX_NOW issues
├─ Phase 4: Fix [Code agent × N]
<!-- compliance:on -->
├─ Phase 5: Write resolution-summary.md (compaction safety; Tracked = "(pending)" or "(pending — TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED)" if manage-debt degrades)
<!-- compliance:off -->
├─ Phase 5: Write the local resolution-summary.md (compaction safety; Tracked = "local")
<!-- compliance:end -->
├─ Phase 6: Polish
├─ Phase 7: Verification Gate [Validate agent, haiku] + push + Fix agent validation-fix loop ≤2
├─ Phase 8: CI Status Gate (conditional)
<!-- compliance:on -->
├─ Phase 9: Git agent (manage-debt) — FIX_SEPARATE + TECH_DEBT → backfill Tracked={ISSUE_REF} (or TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED on failure)
<!-- compliance:end -->
│
<!-- compliance:on -->
├─ Phase 9b: 9b-0 Test agent (stale TPs), 9b-1/9b-2 Git agent (threads, resolution comment)
│  └─ Step 9b-3: verify-evidence.cjs publish (inline, no Git spawn) — only when the head moved
<!-- compliance:off -->
├─ Phase 9b: 9b-0 Test agent (stale TPs, local evidence file)
│  └─ Step 9b-3: verify-evidence.cjs verify (inline, no Git spawn) — local result file, only when the head moved
<!-- compliance:end -->
│
<!-- compliance:on -->
├─ Phase 9c: verify-evidence.cjs readiness (inline, no Git spawn) — non-author approval required, report-only
<!-- compliance:off -->
├─ Phase 9c: verify-evidence.cjs readiness (inline, no Git spawn) — every cycle, local readiness file, report-only
<!-- compliance:end -->
│
└─ Phase 10: Display results (resolution-summary.md written in Phase 5)
```

## Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|------|----------|
| No reviews exist | Check bug-analysis fallback (Step 0c-5b); if also absent, error and suggest `/code-review` or `/bug-analysis` |
| Fix attempt fails | Revert changes, mark BLOCKED, continue others |
| Issue dependencies | Sequential chain, skip dependents if predecessor blocked |
| No issues parsed | Report "No issues to resolve" |
| `--review {timestamp}` in multi-worktree mode | Not supported — use `--path` + `--review` to target specific worktree + review |
<!-- compliance:on -->
| gh/GitHub absent | manage-debt degrades (`TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED ({reason})`); Tracked stays `(pending — TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED ({reason}))` — recorded, not dropped |
| `EVIDENCE_POLICY` is `standard` | Phases 1b and 9b-step-1 are skipped; post-resolution-summary (Phase 9b step 2) still runs if a PR is known |
| `REQUIRE_NON_AUTHOR_APPROVAL` is `false` | Phase 9c is skipped and reported as SKIPPED |
| `reviewPublication: off` | Git agent skips posting the resolution comment (OFF) — except that, only when `EVIDENCE_POLICY` is `required`, Step 0d passes `stub` and a counts-only STUB comment posts |
| Fork PR this run cannot push to | `TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED (cannot push to fork)` → `fork_no_push`: no push in Phase 7, Phase 8 skipped, 9b-1 records FIXED threads as DEGRADED, 9b-2 still posts; the head did not move, so 9b-0 and 9b-3 are skipped |
| The PR has no trusted evidence record | 9b-0 finds no vouched-for stale line, so no Test agent runs; 9b-3 still refreshes the block and comment, every TP without a claim reading `UNVERIFIED` |
<!-- compliance:off -->
| `REQUIRE_NON_AUTHOR_APPROVAL` is `false` | Phase 9c still runs, with `--require-non-author-approval false` |
| Fork PR this run cannot push to | `TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED (cannot push to fork)` → `fork_no_push`: no push in Phase 7, Phase 8 skipped; the head did not move, so 9b-0 and 9b-3 are skipped |
| No local evidence file exists | `STALE_REVERIFICATION` and `EVIDENCE_REFRESH` are `SKIPPED (no local evidence file)`; Phase 9c runs readiness without `--evidence` |
<!-- compliance:end -->
| A CI run behind a claim has expired (~90 days) | The TP reads `INDETERMINATE` — never verified, never failed — until a claim at a newer SHA settles it |

## Principles

1. **Orchestration only** - Command spawns agents, doesn't do git/resolve work itself
2. **Git agent for git work** - All git operations go through Git agent; inline scripts are plumbing
<!-- compliance:on -->
3. **Traceability-aware** - Policy-gated ops are skipped cleanly when the evidence policy does not ask for them; resolution comment (Phase 9b-2) is always-on; test-plan evidence is re-verified (≤1 Test agent) and refreshed only when this run moved the head (Steps 9b-0, 9b-3)
<!-- compliance:off -->
3. **Local evidence** - Nothing is posted: test-plan evidence is re-verified (≤1 Test agent) and verified into a local result file only when this run moved the head (Steps 9b-0, 9b-3); merge readiness is written to a local file on every cycle (Phase 9c)
<!-- compliance:end -->

## Output Artifact

Written in Phase 5 to `{TARGET_DIR}/resolution-summary.md`:

```markdown
# Resolution Summary

**Branch**: {branch} -> {base_branch}
**Date**: {RESOLUTION_TS}
**Review**: {TARGET_DIR_REL}
**Command**: /resolve
**Gate level**: {GATE_LEVEL, with any level note}

<!-- curation:on -->
## Decisions Citations

- {decision applied or pitfall avoided, stated in words — never its ID} — {batch-id}, {issue-id}

(Omit section if no citations were made)

<!-- curation:end -->
## Statistics
| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Total Issues | {n} |
| Fixed | {n} |
| False Positive | {n} |
| By Design | {n} |
| Deferred | {n} |
| Blocked | {n} |
| Escalated | {n} |
| Duplicates Collapsed | {n} |

_(Note: `Deferred` = `## Fix Separately` count + `## Deferred to Tech Debt` count combined — the two sections are distinct by scope, but the Statistics row aggregates both for the convergence parser. `Total Issues` counts every triaged issue including collapsed duplicates; every row **between** `Total Issues` and `Duplicates Collapsed` counts UNIQUE (non-DUPLICATE) issues only, so `Total Issues` equals the sum of the rows below it. Excluding duplicates from `Fixed`, `False Positive`, and `Deferred` de-skews the fp\_ratio convergence formula in code-review without any parser change.)_

## Verification
| Command | Result |
|---------|--------|
| {build/typecheck/lint/test} | PASS \| FAIL |

Regression tests added: {n}

Final gate: {the value Phase 7 recorded}

## Fixed Issues
| Issue | File:Line | Commit |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {sha} |

## False Positives
| Issue | File:Line | Reasoning |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {why} |

## By Design
| Issue | File:Line | Rationale (decision/doc) |
|-------|-----------|--------------------------|
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {the decision, in words, or code comment} |

## Fix Separately
| Issue | File:Line | Reason | Tracked |
|-------|-----------|--------|---------|
<!-- compliance:on -->
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {why out of scope} | {ISSUE_REF} |
<!-- compliance:off -->
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {why out of scope} | local |
<!-- compliance:end -->

## Deferred to Tech Debt
| Issue | File:Line | Risk Factor |
|-------|-----------|-------------|
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {architectural concern} |

## Escalations
| Issue | File:Line | Security Concern |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {why escalated} |

## Blocked
| Issue | File:Line | Blocker |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| {description} | {file}:{line} | {why} |

## Duplicates
| Issue | Duplicate Of | File:Line |
|-------|-------------|-----------|
| {description} | {primary-id} | {file}:{line} |
<!-- compliance:on -->

## Third-Party Threads
| Thread | File:Line | Verdict | Status |
|--------|-----------|---------|--------|
| ext-{N} | {file}:{line} | {FIXED \| FALSE_POSITIVE \| BY_DESIGN \| ESCALATED} | {RESOLVED \| REPLIED \| DEGRADED} |
<!-- compliance:end -->
```
<!-- compliance:on -->

_(Omit `## Third-Party Threads` unless `EVIDENCE_POLICY` is `required` and external threads were found.)_
<!-- compliance:end -->

**Statistics mapping (parser contract)**: the `Deferred` row = FIX_SEPARATE + TECH_DEBT (both deferral dispositions combined); By Design and Escalated are counted separately and excluded from `Deferred`. The `Duplicates Collapsed` row is additive — the `/code-review` convergence parser reads only `Deferred`, `Fixed`, and `False Positive` rows plus `## Fixed Issues` / `## False Positives` headings — keep those labels byte-stable. All rows that the parser reads count UNIQUE (non-DUPLICATE) issues only, so collapsed duplicates do not inflate fp\_ratio.
